==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|hursaz|horse}} (perhaps from a form ''*hrussa-'' ‘runner, racer’), from {{proto|Indo-European|kers-|run}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian ''hors'', Old Saxon [[hros]] (Dutch [[ros]]), Old High German [[hros]], [[ros]] (German [[Ross]]), Old Norse {{term|hross|lang=non}} (whence the Old Swedish ''hors'' and Icelandic {{term|hross||a horse|lang=is}}); and, outside the Germanic languages, with Latin {{term|curro|currō|run, race|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hoɹs/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{infl|ang|noun|n||plural|hors}}

# a [[horse]]

